          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.659,
            0.359,
            0.677
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pause and Ponder"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.688,
            0.861,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Ravi suddenly notices that he is growing taller rapidly, his shoulders are broadening, and his voice cracks. What stage of life is he entering?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.722,
            0.861,
            0.755
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Rina’s period occurs every 28 days. Her last period was on the 5th of March. On which day is she most likely to get her next period?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.757,
            0.747,
            0.774
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. A human zygote has just formed. How many chromosomes does it have?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.799,
            0.644,
            0.817
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11.5.8 Mother’s health during pregnancy"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.82,
            0.89,
            0.922
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A woman’s health during pregnancy plays a vital role in the baby’s growth and safety. She should eat a balanced diet rich in proteins, vitamins and minerals, attend regular medical check-ups, and follow her doctor’s advice regarding light exercise and rest. Her emotional well-being is also important, and support from family members helps her remain healthy and stress-free."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
